  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Give-and-go and drop to the shooter",
  "description": "Two queues, A and B, a little inside the centre line. Goalkeeper in goal. A starts with the ball.\n\nA plays a give-and-go with B and takes the return at speed. Then A slows down while B speeds up and skates in behind A. A drops the ball back to B, who arrives at full speed and shoots. A keeps going towards goal to pick up any rebound.\n\nSwap queues after each go. Progression: a defender starts from the penalty area and tries to disrupt, so A has to choose between the drop pass and going alone. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep your distance – if B gets too close to A there is no room to shoot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Drop the ball clearly backwards so B can choose to shoot first time or take another stride."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "B times the run: behind A just as the ball is dropped."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "A always follows up for the rebound."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "main",
  "difficulty": 3,
